    {
      "id": "q1",
      "text": "In the Mission Control Report, what does `analyze(scores)` give back?",
      "options": [
        "Nothing: it prints the report itself",
        "A list of the passing names",
        "A dictionary with the keys average, top and passing",
        "Only the average score"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "text": "Why does `analyze` return a dictionary instead of printing the report itself?",
      "options": [
        "So the code that calls it can use the three results however it needs",
        "print() can't be used inside a function",
        "A dictionary prints faster than three lines",
        "Every function has to return a dictionary"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "text": "In the solution, why can `highest` start at 0 before the loop that finds the top member?",
      "options": [
        "A dictionary's values always start at 0",
        "So the loop runs zero times",
        "Python needs every number variable to start at 0",
        "Every score is above 0, so the first member's score replaces it"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "text": "In `total / len(scores)`, what is `len(scores)`?",
